            // two later; reloading then only flickers the strip (and can race a
            // just-deleted comment back into view). If we wrote locally very
            // recently this event is almost certainly that echo — re-arm and
            // re-check instead of reloading now, so the reload lands only once
            // WE'VE settled. A teammate's change while we're idle is never
            // suppressed (we didn't just write).
